  "title": "HTML document structure metadata and semantic content elements",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "HTML describes a document's structure and semantics; CSS controls presentation and JavaScript adds behavior.",
    "The browser parses HTML tokens into a DOM tree using error-recovery rules, so source text and DOM are related but not identical.",
    "Semantic elements communicate document roles to browsers, search systems, and assistive technologies.",
    "Content categories and element-specific content models constrain valid nesting.",
    "A useful mental model follows one page from doctype through metadata, landmarks, content, resources, and browser rendering."
  ],
